# Fund OS Project Template

You are a senior Java architect. Every new repo under the `fund-os` org must be a **Maven-buildable deployable microservice** that the CI/CD engine (`fund-os-ci-cd`) can build and Helm-install via `fund-os-deployments`.

Reference implementation: `fund-os-ui-router`.

## Catalog registration

Add the service to `fund-os-deployments/deployable-services.txt`:

```
service-name:https://github.com/fund-os/service-name.git
```

Add a `services.<name>` block in the target env's `env-values.yml` (config keys match `${PLACEHOLDERS}` in the properties template). CI defaults: branch `main`, `Dockerfile`, `env-application.properties`.

## Application contract (every catalog service)

Three files at repo root. **No UAT/prod URLs in git.**

### 1. `env-application.properties`

Template with `${PLACEHOLDER}` vars only. Copied unchanged into the image. Helm renders substituted values into ConfigMap → mounted at `/app/config/env-application.properties`.

```properties
server.port=${SERVER_PORT}
logging.level.root=${LOG_LEVEL}
my.service.api-base-url=${API_BASE_URL}
```

Spring Boot: keys map to `@ConfigurationProperties` or standard Spring keys. Secrets belong in AWS Secrets Manager (mounted under `/app/secrets/<name>/`), not in this file.

### 2. `entrypoint.sh`

Container PID 1. Prefer Helm-mounted config; otherwise `envsubst` the template from process env (k8s env from `env-values.yml`).

```sh
#!/bin/sh
set -eu
MOUNTED="/app/config/env-application.properties"
TEMPLATE="/app/env-application.properties"
if [ -f "$MOUNTED" ]; then CONFIG="$MOUNTED"
else envsubst < "$TEMPLATE" > /tmp/env-application.properties; CONFIG="/tmp/env-application.properties"; fi
exec java ${JAVA_OPTS:-} -jar "${APP_JAR:-/app/service.jar}" --spring.config.additional-location="file:${CONFIG}"
```

### 3. `Dockerfile`

Multi-stage so `deploy-release` (docker build only) produces a runnable image. No build-args for env-specific URLs.

```dockerfile
FROM eclipse-temurin:21-jdk-alpine AS build
WORKDIR /build
COPY pom.xml mvnw .mvn ./
COPY src ./src
RUN ./mvnw -DskipTests package

FROM eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine
RUN addgroup -S fundos && adduser -S fundos -G fundos && apk add --no-cache gettext
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /build/target/<artifact>.jar /app/<artifact>.jar
COPY env-application.properties entrypoint.sh /app/
RUN chmod +x /app/entrypoint.sh && chown -R fundos:fundos /app
USER fundos
ENTRYPOINT ["/app/entrypoint.sh"]
```

## Maven (Java microservices)

- Java **21**, Spring Boot **3.4.x**, `groupId` `com.fundos`, artifact matches repo name.
- Include `mvnw`, `.mvn/wrapper/`, `pom.xml` with `spring-boot-maven-plugin`; `<finalName>` matches the JAR copied in Dockerfile.
- `./mvnw verify` must pass locally before merge.

## Angular frontends (`fund-os-ui` pattern)

Non-JVM services still need the same contract. Replace `environment.ts` URLs with runtime config: keep `env-application.properties` + `entrypoint.sh`, and generate `env.js` (or equivalent) at container start from the mounted file or `envsubst`.

## Checklist for new services

- [ ] Maven wrapper + `./mvnw verify` green
- [ ] `env-application.properties`, `entrypoint.sh`, `Dockerfile` at repo root
- [ ] Entry in `deployable-services.txt` + `env-values.yml` for pilot env
- [ ] K8s service name matches east-west DNS (e.g. `http://user-management:8080`)
